What is a common cause of buffer overflow vulnerabilities in Windows programs? >  Lack of proper bounds checking on user input.

Which programming language commonly used in Windows development is susceptible to buffer overflow vulnerabilities? > C/C++

What technique involves analyzing program binaries to identify potential buffer overflow vulnerabilities without access to source code? > Static analysis

In a Windows stack overflow exploit, what is typically overwritten with a malicious address to redirect program execution to attacker-controlled code? > EIP Register

Which of the following Windows security features can help mitigate the impact of stack overflow exploits by preventing the execution of code in certain memory regions?> DEP

Which technique is commonly used to exploit SEH overflows in Windows systems by corrupting exception handling structures? > SEH overwrite chaining

In a Windows SEH overflow exploit, what data structure is typically overwritten with a malicious address to redirect program execution? > Exception Handler Address
